    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pălaestē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παλαιστή</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a seaport in Epirus</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 3,
				6 <i>fin.</i></span></i> dub. (al.
			Pharsalia).—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pălaestīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Palœste</i> or <i>Epirus</i> (as the entrance to the Lower World), <i>Palœstian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Palaestinae deae,</span>”
				<i>the Furies</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 236</span></i>
			 (where Meletinas is a better reading): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					5, 460</span></i>
			.</div>
